    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "here's the text: \"Section 4.2: Price Adjustments. While the baseline rate is fixed for the duration of the contract, the Supplier reserves the right to implement a seasonal adjustment of up to 5% during peak demand months (June-August) to account for market volatility. Such adjustments shall be applied automatically to all invoices issued during these months.\"\n\nbasically, does this mean they can just change the price whenever they want? i really need to know if we're protected from sudden cost increases here.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
